/T (Moving average forecasting was selected because the business currently relies largely on experience and observation for stocking and procurement decisions. The method provides a simple quantitative estimate of near-future demand using the sales records available from the business. By smoothing random fluctuations in transactional demand, it can support more structured procurement decisions and help reduce unnecessary overstocking and stockouts. This directly supports the second business problem of minimizing total inventory cost. )
