326 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (In Table 2, The ABC classification shows that the revenue contribution is highly concentrated among a small number of products. Class A consists of only 3 products \(12.50% of the total products\), but contributes 67.56% of total revenue, with Suit Piece, Saree, and Dupatta being the major contributors. Class B contains 5 products and contributes 22.30% of revenue, representing products with moderate financial importance. In contrast, Class C contains 16 products \(66.67% of the product range\) but contributes only 10.14% of total revenue. This indicates that inventory management should give greater attention to high-revenue Class A products, while the stock levels of the large number of Class C products should be reviewed carefully to reduce the possibility of unnecessary working capital being tied up in low-contribution inventory.)
