/Title (This pattern provides a clear visual indication that the business has a relatively small group of high-impact products and a much larger group of low-revenue-contributing products. From an inventory-management perspective, this means that stock availability and replenishment decisions for the first few high-revenue products should receive greater attention. At the same time, the large number of Class C products should be reviewed carefully to avoid unnecessary accumulation of slow-moving inventory and consequent locking of working capital.)
